WEBVTT

00:33.260 --> 00:35.750
I can't live with you
any more. Good bye.

00:35.800 --> 00:37.060
Love, Emily

01:19.270 --> 01:21.940
The victim is Robin Hendrix, age 28.

01:22.940 --> 01:24.000
No external wounds.

01:24.180 --> 01:26.770
The estimated time of death,
about 16 hours ago.

01:27.250 --> 01:28.910
Seems he died of natural causes.

01:30.880 --> 01:32.880
He had a visitor.

01:34.460 --> 01:35.580
A woman.

01:36.120 --> 01:38.110
We'll take finger prints
and check them.

01:38.760 --> 01:40.620
Robin Hendrix?

01:41.300 --> 01:42.960
Yes, the screen actor...

01:43.160 --> 01:45.560
He played an alien prince
in his first movie,...

01:45.630 --> 01:48.190
which helped him make
a name for himself.

01:48.370 --> 01:50.390
But, it was more
than ten years ago.

01:52.640 --> 01:54.610
Jill, have this checked as well.

01:55.440 --> 01:56.600
What's this?

02:05.090 --> 02:07.990
All the unsolved, unnatural death
cases in the past few years.

02:08.890 --> 02:10.880
One victim's body
was severely damaged...

02:10.920 --> 02:12.360
as if torn apart by an animal.

02:12.560 --> 02:14.550
Another's was drained
of all its blood.

02:15.860 --> 02:18.130
M.O. and situations
were all different,...

02:18.800 --> 02:20.790
but one common factor was...

02:21.800 --> 02:24.000
all the victims were
customers of D's pet shop.

02:24.870 --> 02:25.700
No luck!

02:25.740 --> 02:26.360
What?

02:26.870 --> 02:29.240
We performed an autopsy
on that little lizard,...

02:29.280 --> 02:31.040
but no poison was discovered.

02:31.640 --> 02:34.380
Besides, it was a rare species
not listed in any reference books.

02:34.410 --> 02:36.710
I guess we don't have
any proof to cite the pet shop...

02:36.750 --> 02:38.480
for violating
the Washington Convention.

02:39.420 --> 02:42.580
As for Robin, there were no
external wounds, or drugs.

02:42.620 --> 02:45.820
The cosmetics scattered around
the room belong to his wife.

02:45.860 --> 02:48.890
They're separated now,
but she has an alibi.

02:48.930 --> 02:51.490
Grudges held by co-workers,
also, seem unlikely.

02:55.570 --> 02:58.660
Leon, you can't adopt
straightforward tactics in Chinatown.

02:58.940 --> 02:59.870
What?

03:00.410 --> 03:02.900
Pull when you want to push.
Understand?

03:09.320 --> 03:11.980
You always show up at tea time.

03:12.550 --> 03:16.650
It's always tea time for you.
How's business?

03:17.360 --> 03:20.550
I can't complain.
What can I do for you?

03:21.260 --> 03:23.700
You've heard about Robin Hendrix?

03:24.100 --> 03:28.260
I saw it on the news.
It's a pity, he was so young.

03:29.070 --> 03:31.300
He was a very good customer of ours.

03:31.570 --> 03:34.910
He'd purchased more than
twenty reptiles total,...

03:34.940 --> 03:37.740
including an iguana,
an anole and various agamid lizards.

03:37.950 --> 03:40.040
It's one of those, isn't it?

03:40.710 --> 03:42.710
We found it dead by the victim.

03:51.760 --> 03:52.780
Dead...

03:54.760 --> 04:00.360
Oh, no. There are only a few
of this species left on earth.

04:01.400 --> 04:03.390
What did you fit it with?

04:04.070 --> 04:06.560
No poison was found
by the autopsy but...

04:08.580 --> 04:15.000
Please, our merchandise is
love and dreams, not poison.

04:16.420 --> 04:19.110
Pull when you want
to push, understand?

04:20.020 --> 04:23.680
I hear Count D has
a sweet tooth, especially for...

04:24.860 --> 04:26.850
Oh, I almost forgot.

04:32.700 --> 04:36.230
This aroma, it must be De Champagne
from the Hotel de Marseilles!

04:36.340 --> 04:40.770
Wow! They bake only 30 pieces a day;
you'd have to go there before...

04:40.810 --> 04:43.300
the bakery opens and stand
in line to get this!

04:43.780 --> 04:45.970
I didn't know you were
such a kind man!

04:51.220 --> 04:53.210
If you ask me...

04:53.390 --> 04:56.190
Robin was possessed
and killed by a spirit.

04:56.920 --> 04:57.820
A spirit?

04:58.390 --> 05:01.880
Ten years ago, he catapulted to
fame with his first movie.

05:02.460 --> 05:05.560
After that, however, he was not
lucky enough to find roles that...

05:05.600 --> 05:07.260
would further expand his career.

05:07.300 --> 05:10.670
Or rather, despite his beauty,
his talent as an actor was lacking.

05:11.570 --> 05:15.300
Yes, the image he established as
an unfortunate Prince who...

05:15.910 --> 05:20.180
sacrificed his life to save
his mother planet was too strong.

05:21.110 --> 05:23.100
People could only
see him as that Prince.

05:23.450 --> 05:26.010
His delicate,
innocent blue eyes and...

05:26.390 --> 05:28.820
platinum blond hair
shining in the light,...

05:35.100 --> 05:39.050
Robin was possessed by the
spirit of the prince he played,...

05:39.630 --> 05:40.960
and was killed by it.

05:42.640 --> 05:44.130
Give me a break.

05:44.200 --> 05:46.200
If spirits could kill people
and get away with it,...

05:46.240 --> 05:48.230
how am I supposed
to stay in business?

05:48.340 --> 05:50.780
Forget it.
When did you see him last?

05:54.820 --> 05:56.810
Please, before it gets cold.

05:56.950 --> 05:57.940
When was it?

06:01.320 --> 06:05.020
As I recall, about two months ago.

06:05.490 --> 06:06.790
Hey Count!

06:07.130 --> 06:09.560
Welcome, His Imperial Highness
the Crown Prince.

06:09.630 --> 06:12.430
Hey, D, don't use that name.

06:12.930 --> 06:15.530
Excuse me,
I did not mean any offense.

06:16.400 --> 06:19.100
You want the usual food
for your little friends?

06:19.240 --> 06:23.270
No, I figured I'd get another one,
something rare and new.

06:23.780 --> 06:27.440
But if I'm not mistaken,
you promised Her Imperial Highness...

06:27.480 --> 06:29.470
not to get any more pets.

06:30.050 --> 06:34.150
Yeah, but Her Imperial Highness
has left me.

06:35.520 --> 06:38.650
She thinks I should
marry a lizard or snake.

06:39.430 --> 06:44.230
Now, I'm free to keep my pets
in my living room or bedroom.

06:45.570 --> 06:46.660
Your Highness.

06:58.280 --> 07:01.250
Something special just
came in the other day.

07:01.550 --> 07:03.280
Would you like to take a look?

07:06.720 --> 07:07.710
Please.

07:08.520 --> 07:12.150
My goodness! I didn't know
you had an opium den.

07:12.630 --> 07:17.000
Now please, this is a pet shop.

07:27.010 --> 07:29.000
Please watch your step.

07:44.360 --> 07:45.590
Here it is.

07:51.230 --> 07:54.890
Since you are our special customer,
I'll sell it to you if you like it.

08:06.310 --> 08:07.710
What do you think?

08:07.910 --> 08:12.850
D, it's a bad joke.
Even though my wife just left me.

08:13.350 --> 08:15.620
Your Highness,
please look carefully.

08:19.290 --> 08:21.160
It's a lizard.

08:21.860 --> 08:25.590
A subspecies of a very rare kind,
and an albino on top of that.

08:25.630 --> 08:27.620
It's a valuable find, indeed.

08:32.970 --> 08:34.740
Am I dreaming?

08:35.480 --> 08:39.270
Touch it and find out yourself.

08:44.080 --> 08:45.680
Don't worry.

08:47.950 --> 08:48.940
OK.

08:56.930 --> 08:58.450
No, it can't be...

09:03.340 --> 09:05.000
Oh, yes, it is...

09:05.110 --> 09:07.970
This cold, smooth skin...

09:12.780 --> 09:16.410
Why is she blindfolded?

09:17.380 --> 09:19.380
Let me see the eyes.

09:19.690 --> 09:22.120
I'm afraid that's not possible.

09:22.520 --> 09:24.790
Why?
Is she injured?

09:25.660 --> 09:31.530
No. However, you can never
take it off under any circumstances.

09:32.100 --> 09:35.160
Why?
Please let me see her face.

09:35.770 --> 09:36.860
Please!

09:38.370 --> 09:41.340
The legend has it
that this species...

09:41.810 --> 09:44.740
were kept as weapons
for assassination.

09:45.650 --> 09:47.240
Is she poisonous?

09:47.950 --> 09:51.780
You know it is not uncommon
for some reptiles to have poisons...

09:52.380 --> 09:54.150
but it's something else.

09:54.220 --> 09:57.050
Something that should be
referred to as a magical power.

09:57.660 --> 09:58.780
A magical power!?

09:58.990 --> 10:01.860
Yes, according to
ancient Greek myths.

10:05.930 --> 10:08.870
A king was defeated in battle and
escaped the field to save his life.

10:08.900 --> 10:11.530
When the enemy soldiers spotted him,
they ran over to him.

10:13.810 --> 10:19.680
However, what the soldiers saw
was a beautiful woman.

10:50.880 --> 10:54.570
She made them drop their guard
with her enchanting body,...

10:54.610 --> 10:57.950
and when they saw her eyes,
they all turned into stone, instantly.

10:58.620 --> 11:01.990
That's the power
of this species, Medusa.

11:11.100 --> 11:13.190
No way could that be possible!

11:13.700 --> 11:16.260
That's what Robin
said at first as well.

11:16.740 --> 11:19.140
First of all, if he thought
a lizard was a human woman,...

11:19.170 --> 11:21.640
he must have been
on drugs or something.

11:22.070 --> 11:25.410
I am merely telling you the truth.

11:26.380 --> 11:29.440
Whether you believe it
or not is your choice.

11:31.250 --> 11:32.620
Stop playing with me!

11:32.950 --> 11:35.390
Why don't you get
something for yourself?

11:36.060 --> 11:37.080
I'd recommend...

11:37.120 --> 11:39.020
...a Java sparrow right there.

11:39.260 --> 11:41.750
I don't need any pets!

11:42.160 --> 11:45.390
No, what I'm suggesting is that
you grind it and eat its bones.

11:46.570 --> 11:49.540
You are so irritable you must
suffer from calcium deficiency.

11:54.540 --> 11:55.840
You win.

11:59.140 --> 12:02.340
And after all that,
Robin bought the lizard?

12:02.720 --> 12:06.550
Yes. The lizard seemed
to like Robin, too.

12:07.390 --> 12:11.410
I could not interfere with her
choice of companion.

12:12.590 --> 12:15.890
Here's the contract.
Would you care to read it?

12:18.100 --> 12:20.090
There are three sales terms.

12:20.330 --> 12:23.630
(1) The customer is to feed her
fresh fruits or small live animals...

12:23.670 --> 12:25.330
on a daily basis.

12:26.010 --> 12:29.460
(2) The customer is
not to show her to anybody.

12:29.980 --> 12:34.000
(3) The customer is not to look into
her eyes under any circumstances.

12:34.710 --> 12:37.050
Should any of
these terms be breached,...

12:37.080 --> 12:39.850
the pet shop will not assume any
responsibilities for any consequences.

12:40.690 --> 12:42.850
If this is acceptable,
please sign the contract.

12:44.460 --> 12:48.620
I need to take this
and give it to a graphology lab.

12:49.230 --> 12:50.350
As you wish.

12:51.560 --> 12:55.360
By the way,
Robin Hendrix's manager told us...

12:56.440 --> 12:59.500
...that he went for an audition
held by some movie company...

12:59.540 --> 13:01.370
two weeks prior to his death.

13:01.840 --> 13:04.640
As he hadn't done anything
special for so long,...

13:05.710 --> 13:09.880
I figured a bad actor like him
would give up on his dreams.

13:10.450 --> 13:13.580
Well, I think not.

13:14.450 --> 13:16.150
Why do you say that?

13:16.360 --> 13:21.520
Don't you see?
He already had another dream.

13:22.160 --> 13:23.420
Another dream?

13:23.730 --> 13:26.530
Yes, a new raison d'Ã©tre.

13:31.770 --> 13:33.760
Do you like it, Medusa?

13:36.070 --> 13:38.840
Even though she can't talk,
I'd rather have her than...

13:38.880 --> 13:40.740
those screaming, hysterical women.

13:42.520 --> 13:44.450
It doesn't matter if she can't see.

13:44.480 --> 13:47.680
She's nothing like those who
are only interested in my looks.

13:48.950 --> 13:51.250
She's not one of those
annoying fans, either.

13:51.360 --> 13:56.490
The most important thing is that
she can't live without me.

13:58.100 --> 14:00.400
She can't live
without my protection.

14:01.470 --> 14:06.430
Medusa, please, live only for me.

14:19.280 --> 14:22.780
Hey Albert.
Yeah, I'm doing OK.

14:23.560 --> 14:29.500
About the audition...
Yeah, right, it's not a big role.

14:29.930 --> 14:31.950
But, you can'tjust sit there
and wait for something...

14:32.000 --> 14:33.190
to come your way.

14:33.870 --> 14:38.630
You know that too, don't you?
You can't be the Crown Prince forever.

14:38.870 --> 14:40.860
This might be your last chance.

14:41.670 --> 14:43.900
Our contract is about to expire,
and we can't renew it...

14:43.940 --> 14:45.380
unless you get this role.

14:45.540 --> 14:49.110
Besides, without your wife's money,
you can't keep...

14:49.150 --> 14:51.410
that gorgeous apartment.

14:51.850 --> 14:55.720
You will have to get rid
of your precious pets.

14:56.490 --> 14:57.420
Right?

14:58.390 --> 15:00.660
Well, give me a call if you want
to go for this audition.

15:00.690 --> 15:01.450
Bye.

15:20.180 --> 15:23.810
OK. Let's take a break.
We'll do another take in 5 minutes.

15:25.750 --> 15:27.010
You were great, Robin!

15:27.050 --> 15:29.040
You're already in
the final selection.

15:29.590 --> 15:32.350
Those amateurs didn't
even compare to you.

15:32.790 --> 15:34.780
The producer's impressed, too.

15:35.460 --> 15:37.430
Now, we can show them
what you can do!

15:37.460 --> 15:39.450
Those backbiters who said
you were a one hit wonder.

15:39.630 --> 15:41.960
Oh, sorry.

15:42.900 --> 15:44.890
That's OK.
It doesn't bother me.

15:45.140 --> 15:50.730
Well, but I'm happy you
are finally motivated.

15:51.840 --> 15:54.010
The only thing now
is to beat that guy...

15:56.420 --> 16:00.880
Toby Highmer,
the up-and-coming musical star.

16:02.790 --> 16:04.780
Don't let me down.

16:14.270 --> 16:15.890
Take three, get set!

16:22.440 --> 16:25.880
I'm not made for competition,
but it's been so long since...

16:26.210 --> 16:28.740
I felt so energized.

16:31.620 --> 16:34.180
I feel alive.

16:51.840 --> 16:58.270
I didn't know Highmer's manager
was the producer's lover, either.

16:59.410 --> 17:01.210
That's OK, Albert.

17:01.480 --> 17:02.640
Just forget it.

17:04.150 --> 17:06.140
I just don't have what it takes.

17:06.650 --> 17:10.320
That's not true! I promise you,
I will get a great role for you.

17:11.020 --> 17:12.890
Here, get in. I'll drive you home.

17:13.260 --> 17:14.950
No, I have to go.

17:16.730 --> 17:18.560
Thanks for everything, Albert.

17:19.470 --> 17:21.460
Hey Robin! Hey! Wait!

17:23.300 --> 17:24.390
Robin...

17:56.740 --> 18:02.300
I'm sorry. I'm such a loser
I can't even protect you.

18:04.040 --> 18:05.870
I'm so sorry.

18:11.880 --> 18:13.870
You are so beautiful, Medusa.

18:17.520 --> 18:19.250
Let's toast.

18:21.390 --> 18:24.290
Though it's a small party,
we are going to celebrate the day.

18:24.700 --> 18:26.260
Just you and me...

18:30.500 --> 18:31.940
Today...

18:32.200 --> 18:34.200
is going to be my anniversary.

18:41.710 --> 18:43.410
Look at me.

18:45.920 --> 18:47.980
I want you to look at me.

18:50.860 --> 18:54.790
It's OK.
Don't be afraid.

19:31.300 --> 19:32.420
Impossible!

19:32.500 --> 19:34.990
No lizard can kill
a human with its gaze!

19:35.840 --> 19:42.300
Then, there is no proof that
we sold a dangerous pet, either.

19:46.910 --> 19:50.280
Thank you for stopping by.
Please leave now.

19:51.120 --> 19:55.250
Hey, wait! What about Medusa?
Why did she have to die, too?

19:57.320 --> 20:00.520
What does the body
of the white lizard mean?

20:02.060 --> 20:06.460
To tell you the truth,
I did not expect her to follow him.

20:06.930 --> 20:08.060
However,...

20:08.870 --> 20:13.830
the man she loved died when
she saw him for the first time.

20:14.910 --> 20:16.900
Died because of her eyes.

20:22.350 --> 20:26.480
In her sorrow, she probably
looked at them herself.

20:30.020 --> 20:31.720
She looked at her own eyes.

20:35.290 --> 20:38.490
She killed herself
for her love of him.

20:40.800 --> 20:42.790
Robin's heart was still
as innocent as a little boy's.

20:43.400 --> 20:53.870
What he saw in Medusa's eyes was...
a sweet darkness called despair.

20:56.150 --> 20:58.670
A wise child is
the joy of the father.

20:59.480 --> 21:02.280
A foolish child is
the sorrow of the mother.

21:03.960 --> 21:09.720
Material wealth is of no meaning;
justice is what saves man.

21:10.330 --> 21:13.730
Medusa's bones.
I thought the lovers...

21:13.770 --> 21:15.860
would want to rest together.

21:16.940 --> 21:18.230
Whatever.

21:19.340 --> 21:22.930
But, Robin is finally free,
don't you think?

21:23.410 --> 21:25.500
What good does it do him now?

21:25.540 --> 21:26.640
He's dead.

21:27.180 --> 21:30.840
I wouldn't say that...look.

21:31.650 --> 21:33.710
But still,
he was too young to die.

21:33.750 --> 21:35.740
His first movie was a piece of art.

21:35.790 --> 21:37.780
An actor with such talents...

21:37.960 --> 21:41.220
I hear he had another
movie starting soon.

21:41.330 --> 21:42.730
He was a genius.

21:42.800 --> 21:45.020
Whom the gods love, die young.

21:45.060 --> 21:47.050
This is a big loss
to the entire movie industry.

21:47.100 --> 21:49.070
I hoped he'd make a comeback.

21:49.230 --> 21:50.330
See?

21:50.770 --> 21:53.300
Rather than getting old
and wasting his life...

21:53.340 --> 21:56.140
in the ugly world of show business.

21:57.210 --> 22:00.180
He chose to live a short,
spectacular life and to die before...

22:00.210 --> 22:01.840
he woke up from his dreams.

22:02.780 --> 22:08.050
A new, ever-lasting legend
of a movie star is born.
